# The ledger

The ledger is the annals of this project. Each entry records one change of
state in the repository: what we set out to do, what we arrived at, what was
decided, and where we went off course. An entry is written when the change
is committed, and it goes into the same commit.

The ledger differs from its neighbours in one way: it is never brought up to
date. A [story](../stories/index.hmd) is edited as the work moves, so it
always says where things stand now. A ledger entry says where things stood
on its day and is left as written. A mistake in an entry is corrected by a
dated note at its end, or by a later entry.

| Document | Says | Changes afterwards |
|---|---|---|
| Story | what is being invented and where it stands | yes, kept current |
| Proposal | one decision, before it is taken | its status only |
| Discussion | what each agent said and did in one session | entries are added |
| Ledger | what one change of state amounted to, and what was decided for good | no |

## Naming

An entry is one file, named by the date of its commit and a short name for
the change.

```
YYYY-MM-DD-name-of-the-change.hmd
```

Two entries on one day are told apart by their names.

## Parts of an entry

1. **The change.** The branch, the commit it follows, and its size.
2. **Objectives.** What we set out to do, in the words of the time.
3. **Arrived at.** Where the repository stands after the change.
4. **Accomplished.** What was built, by whom.
5. **Decisions.** What was decided for good, each with who decided it. This
   is the part later readers come for.
6. **Sidetracks.** Where we left the path, what it cost, and what it taught.
7. **Not done.** What the objectives asked for and the change does not hold.

